  "question": {
    "text": "A coil of cross-sectional area <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> having&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math> turns is placed in a uniform magnetic field <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>. When it is rotated with an angular velocity <math><mi>&#969;,</mi></math> the maximum e.m.f. induced in the coil will be:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>n</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>&#969;</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>n</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>&#969;</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mi>n</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>ω</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>n</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>&#969;</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Magnetic flux through a coil of area&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>&nbsp;turns at an angle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi></math>&nbsp;to the magnetic field of magnitude&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;is,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#966;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi></math>. The induced emf,<br /><br /><math><mi>&#949;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>&#981;</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>&#969;</mi><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sin</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></math>. Since, the maximum value of the sine function is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>,<br /><br /><math><msub><mrow><mi>&#949;</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>&#969;</mi></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
